# oneport-account

**The account & metering client shared by every paid Oneport tool.** Login, token
balance, redeem codes — and the `call_managed_llm()` function tools use to run a
billed model call through the Oneport backend.

No tool ever holds a model key. Each holds only your revocable `op_live_...` token;
the backend meters your balance and calls the model with the server-side key.

## For users

```bash
# 1. Get a token (free signup tokens) at https://oneport.dev, then:
oneport-account login op_live_xxxxxxxxxxxx      # or: op account login ...
oneport-account balance                         # tokens remaining + usage by tool
oneport-account redeem LAUNCH2026               # redeem a free-token code
oneport-account logout
```

When a tool runs out of tokens it prints a buy link; top up on the website and keep
going. Codes grant free tokens (great for launches, students, design partners).

## For tool authors

```python
from oneport_account import call_managed_llm, OutOfTokens, NotLoggedIn

try:
    result = call_managed_llm(system, user, tool="apidiff", action="classify")
    text, tokens, balance = result.text, result.tokens_used, result.balance
except NotLoggedIn:
    ...   # tell the user to `oneport-account login`
except OutOfTokens as e:
    ...   # show e.buy_url
```

`call_managed_llm` raises `NotLoggedIn`, `OutOfTokens` (with `.buy_url`),
`RateLimited`, or `AccountError` — map these onto your tool's own taxonomy.

## Configuration

The backend URL resolves as: `$ONEPORT_API_URL` → the value pinned at login →
`DEFAULT_API_URL` in `config.py` (set this to your Supabase Edge Functions base
URL once, e.g. `https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1`).

The token is stored at `~/.oneport/credentials.json` (0600 where supported).

## Privacy

Deterministic work in every tool stays local. Only the LLM judgment call routes
through the proxy so it can be metered — and only the already-computed prompt
(never your repository) is sent. See each tool's PRIVACY notes.

